        "original_id": "395a2654-14cb-57e4-824a-c083f10bb635",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Whishaw, James Bond, James Bond film producers, Glyn Daniel, Max Mallowan, T. E. Lawrence, Jan Morris\n- Characters: Q, M, Miss Moneypenny, Sir Percy Fawcett, H. Rider Haggard’s Allan Quatermain\n- Organizations: Royal Geographical Society, Secret Intelligence Service, MI6\n- Works: Skyfall, Spectre, Quartermain of the Quarter Sessions, Last of the Curlews\n- Concepts: fictional inspirations, literary and film influences\n\nFacts:\n- The Royal Geographical Society is a British organization whose fictional head was inspired by a one-time missionary.\n- T. E. Lawrence was a one-time missionary and was cited as an inspiration for the fictional head of the Royal Geographical Society in Glyn Daniel’s 1982 novel Quartermain of the Quarter Sessions.\n- Glyn Daniel based his fictional head of the Royal Geographical Society partly on H. Rider Haggard’s Allan Quatermain and on real explorers including T. E. Lawrence.\n- In the James Bond films Skyfall and Spectre, Ben Whishaw played the character Q.\n- The answer implied by combining these clues is Q, because Ben Whishaw portrayed Q in Skyfall and Spectre.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
